Modifications made in this fork (branch feat/typescript-support)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The upstream project parses Python source with the standard library `ast`
module to build a heterogeneous code graph (dependency_graph/build_graph.py).
This fork adds a parallel TypeScript/TSX front end built on tree-sitter, plus
a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server so the graph-guided retrieval tools can
be used from MCP clients such as Cline.

New files:
  dependency_graph/ts_build_graph.py        - tree-sitter graph builder for .ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx,
                                              plus patch_ts_graph() incremental refresh
  dependency_graph/ts_resolver.py           - TS/TSX module + path-alias import resolution
                                              (JSONC tsconfig, extends chain, baseUrl)
  dependency_graph/ts_bm25.py               - self-contained BM25 index over graph nodes (bm25s)
  dependency_graph/ts_patch_check.py        - patch-vs-rebuild equivalence check (regression guard)
  dependency_graph/ts_edit.py               - structured edits over graph-addressed AST entities
  dependency_graph/ts_edit_check.py         - behaviour check for the edit layer (refusal cases)
  dependency_graph/queries/typescript.scm   - tree-sitter capture queries (typescript grammar)
  dependency_graph/queries/tsx.scm          - tsx-grammar deltas (JSX)
  plugins/location_tools/utils/compress_file_ts.py - tree-sitter skeletonizer (replaces the libcst one for TS)
  locagent_mcp.py                           - FastMCP (stdio) server: graph_search, graph_get,
                                              graph_traverse, graph_map
  requirements-ts.txt                       - minimal runtime dependency set
  NOTICE                                    - this file

